module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_kill_between_the_capture_steps_loses_or_doubles_the_capture

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { NoRungStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

// Consumer: directory-derived recurring_failure_mode.roster, projected by
// gunbc.design_ledgers.expected_design_failure_modes_md through docs_projection_gate.
data a_kill_between_the_capture_steps_loses_or_doubles_the_capture: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_kill_between_the_capture_steps_loses_or_doubles_the_capture" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: NoRungStated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a capture is three effects (scm_persist_capture, commit_staged, the capture-file write) with no durable record that the sequence began, so a belt killed between any two leaves a half capture the next pass cannot recognize. HARM: killed after the SCM save, the retry mints a second capture (double capture); killed after the git commit, the commit exists but no capture file names it (lost capture). Found by PR 14235 slice 3 (DESIGN section 4b) at mitigatable: the old belt_commit_capture_candidate was not resumable.  DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the same code is correct when uninterrupted, so only a kill between steps exposes it; no typecheck or pure witness can reach it.  Cite the red-on-main receipt in the PR 14235 body: the since-deleted belt_capture_intent_red_probe failed both kill points on main (double capture, lost capture).",

    "RUNG NOW: mitigatable. The capture intent (a SubmissionCapture keyed on the pre-commit base head, written before commit_staged outside the submission dir) makes the sequence resumable; belt_capture_intent_complete finishes what is owed, and the ordinal check skips a persist whose SCM save already happened. Executed evidence: test.claim.roadmap.belt_capture_intent_wet_witness passes both kill points on the branch. The invalid interleaving is still writable and safety depends on the intent being written first and the wet witness staying enrolled. CEILING: structurally guaranteed once capture is one typed acquisition whose steps cannot be sequenced without the intent, because the order is decidable and fully modeled; a kill is external reality, so impossibility is out of reach. NEXT TRIGGER: can climb after one grounding, a typed multi-effect capture step in std that refuses an unintented commit.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.roadmap.belt_capture_intent_wet_witness", decl_name: "live_tree_disposition", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_capture_intent_complete", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_commit_capture_candidate", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
